check_ols_single_column_matches_the_closed_form OK [IDENTICAL]: 3.2484779357910156 vs 3.248477637502271 (|delta| 2.982887448155225e-07); the wrong closed form 0.30032332635564307 is distinguishable
check_ols_normal_equation_residual_is_zero OK [IDENTICAL]: ||A^T (A w - b)||_inf 7.79028011805659e-05 <= 0.5092932597037362; the perturbed vector gives 2.3376952948422898
check_ols_duplicating_a_row_equals_doubling_its_weight OK [IDENTICAL]: worst |delta| 9.5367431640625e-07 <= 0.01375846330413849; the unweighted control is 1.714409589767456 away, so the weights demonstrably reached the fit
check_ols_sample_weight_restores_its_operands OK [IDENTICAL]: A within 5.960464477539063e-08, b within 1.4901161193847656e-08, w within 0.0; the scaling itself moves A by 1.9497298002243042
check_ols_sample_weight_host_rescale_matches_device OK [IDENTICAL]: all 5 coefficients byte-identical between ols_fit_weighted_host and the host rescale; a different weight vector moves 5 of them
check_ols_arms_are_pinned OK [IDENTICAL]: step 1 compiles against column bit-identical and the pinned Gram kernel serves 8, 16 and 128 features
check_ols_over_capacity_fits OK [IDENTICAL]: 512 x 130 fits through the whole estimator (worst |w - w*| = 0.00033879280090354236, run-to-run coefficients moved: 0)
check_ols_is_launch_invariant OK [IDENTICAL]: all 12 coefficients bit-identical across elem_tpb 256/64, 0/37 floats of buffer padding and two different scratch poisons (coef[0] = 0xbc0517a9), and the A-vs-A control agrees
check_ols_host_surface_takes_the_guard OK [IDENTICAL]: the Python-facing entry interpolates a 6 x 16 design (residual 2.5087931404543795e-07), i.e. it takes the min-norm route and not lstsq_eig; the 16 x 6 control does not (0.5533459960525986)
